ADR 0005 calls the synchronous DBI usage write 'ticketed', but no open card exists. Maintainer decision: either an async/off-loop write path (design needed) or ADR 0005 says it stays, with jsonlog as the recommendation.

2026-09-30 05:40 Analysis: every Proxy exit path calls _record_usage_event -> usage.record -> store->store BEFORE render, so the client's own answer and every other stream on the loop wait for the DBI insert (autocommit: one commit/fsync per event). Decision: (a) opt-in write-behind in UsageStore::DBI: usage_store.flush_interval_ms (default 0 = today's synchronous insert, unchanged). >0: store() queues and returns {ok=>1, queued=>1}; a Mojo::IOLoop timer flushes the queue in ONE transaction. Batch failure on a live handle -> per-event fallback so one bad event loses only itself; dead handle -> one reconnect per flush, not per event. Lost events reported via a Skeid on_usage_lost hook the proxy logs in the existing 'usage event lost' format. Flush on disconnect (store replaced on reload, DEMOLISH), on no running loop (sync), and an END block in bin/skeid (daemon TERM, prefork graceful). Not fully off-loop: the flush itself still runs on the loop, amortised; truly async needs DBD::Pg pg_async (untestable offline) -- documented in ADR 0005.

